On Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:22:45 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> This is a big commit, and changes a bunch of things. We're basically
> replacing services. Is it possible to break this up into logical
> changes? I would like to see this patch series be more evolutionary,
> than just dumping a big change.

Yes, and thanks for pushing on this. The steps read much better on their
own. v3 is posted as "[PATCH v3 0/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build
the list's mail hub" [1], threaded under v1. It splits this patch
into six, each swapping or adding one piece and leaving a jail that
works:

- "Let Dovecot write the list": vmail owns the maildir, and mbsync
  still fetches one way, but into Dovecot over IMAP as the login
  mbsync. Readers see no change.
- "Sync the list both ways with Fastmail": the fetch becomes a
  two-way sync of lists and Archive.
- "Let Pat archive and delete": your login joins imap-users and the
  ACL.
- "Take posts with OpenSMTPD": OpenSMTPD replaces smtprelay and hands
  posts to Dovecot over LMTP, into INBOX. smtprelay, jq, and the
  mailcred group go.
- "Refuse malformed posts": the check-message filter.
- "Document importing the jj maildir": the README section alone.

The spec fix stays first and the Sieve proposal stays last, both
unchanged. The tree after the six steps is identical to the old patch
2's, so v2's tests still hold for the end state. Between the steps I
could only check script syntax and that dist.mtree matches dist/ at
each one, since Dovecot and smtpd are not installed here.

One thing to know if you apply only part of the series: the first
step is the only one that needs the old maildir and mbsync's state
emptied before the jail restarts. The README in that step says so.

